<%# A host owning the day view. The cells are links, the agenda *is* the frame
    they swap, and the frame's `src` loads it once on connect — so the built-in
    agenda is what a browser without JavaScript is left with, which is the right
    fallback rather than an empty box.

    The route, the model and the frame's markup live in `test/dummy`, because a
    Lookbook preview can render a calendar but cannot answer its links. What
    comes back carries four fields the calendar never had: where, who to ring,
    what state it is in, and the note from last time. %>
<%= render(Shadcn::EventCalendar::Component.new(
      month: Date.new(2026, 8, 1),
      selected: Date.new(2026, 8, 20),
      events: Appointment.for_calendar,
      day_url: ->(date) { "/calendar/days/#{date.iso8601}" },
      day_attributes: { data: { turbo_frame: "day" } },
      agenda_as: :"turbo-frame",
      agenda_attributes: { id: "day", src: "/calendar/days/2026-08-20" }
    )) %>
